 "etapas": [
  {
   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Descriptions and habits",
     "texto": [
      "The imperfect is used to describe the past (**A casa era grande**, the house was big) and to say what you always did (**Morava em Coimbra**, I lived in Coimbra).",
      "It does not say when it started or when it ended. It only describes."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Endings",
     "texto": [
      "For verbs in **-ar**: **-ava** (falava, I used to speak). For verbs in -er and -ir: **-ia** (comia, I used to eat).",
      "«Eu falava, tu falavas, ele falava, nós falávamos, eles falavam. Eu comia, tu comias, ele comia, nós comíamos, eles comiam.»"
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Irregulars",
     "texto": [
      "**Ser** → **era** (was), **ter** → **tinha** (used to have), **ir** → **ia** (used to go).",
      "Watch out: **ia** (used to go) comes from **ir** in the imperfect. **Fui** (I went) is from the one-off past."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
